.TH GIT-@-SHASUM 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-shasum \- Display detailed branch status and commit relationships
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ shasum
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBshasum\fR command provides detailed information about the current branch's commit hash, its relationship to the trunk branch, and recent commit history.
.PP
The command was renamed from the original \fBhash\fR command to avoid conflicts with standard Git commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH INFORMATION DISPLAYED
.TP
.B Current branch name
Name of the currently checked out branch
.TP
.B Current commit hash (SHA)
Full SHA of the current commit
.TP
.B Merge base with trunk branch
Common ancestor commit between current branch and trunk
.TP
.B Number of commits ahead/behind trunk
How many commits the current branch is ahead or behind trunk
.TP
.B Recent commit history
Last 5 commits in the current branch
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show hash information for current branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ shasum
.fi
.RE
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
The command displays information in a formatted table with GitAT styling, making it easy to understand the current branch state.
.SH TRUNK BRANCH DETECTION
.PP
The command attempts to determine the trunk branch in this order:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
Check GitAT configuration (\fBat.trunk\fR)
.IP 2. 3
Check if \fBmain\fR branch exists
.IP 3. 3
Check if \fBmaster\fR branch exists
.IP 4. 3
Fall back to \fBmain\fR as default
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-logz (1),
.BR git (1)